Plan C (AgentX): ISS owns ifTable, so SNMP/AgentX SET ifAdminStatus lands in ISS (`cfa2/src/ifmibwr.c:IfAdminStatusSet`), NOT the net-snmp ies-auto-mibs Flask path (change A skipped ifmibdb). Two things came out of wiring SET→config and observing load behaviour (2026-06-25, branch `snmp-agentx-default-agentx`).

**Q2 — SET ifAdminStatus → config layer (DONE, +21/-2 in ifmibwr.c).** The framework's real SET URI fn is `LibFrameworkUri_PatchUri(handle, uri, token, json, &ret)` (lib `lib_moxa_framework_uri`, in-process HTTP PATCH to 127.0.0.1:80 nginx → config_layer; NOT a shell — `/sbin/ies_uri_handle_client` is the shell variant; `ies_uri_handle_oid_update` is a *different* mechanism = socket IPC to the urihook daemon). Token (`gUriToken`/`security_tokens[]`) is per-SNMPv3-user, minted by `LibUtil_CreateToken(user, service, file)` (`lib_moxa_utility`); AgentX does NOT forward securityName to the subagent, so ISS can't get the per-user token. BUT no need to build any of this: **ISS already wraps it** — `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfg(ifIndex, adminStatus)` and `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfgAsync(...)` in `future/mxcfg/src/portmxcfg.c` do token+handle+GET-modify-PATCH (`gMxCfgToken` auto-minted by mxcfg), already used by TurboRing/TurboChain/loop-protection(lpapi)/port-security/RLPS/goosecheck. Fix = one call in `IfAdminStatusSet` after `nmhSetIfAdminStatus` succeeds: `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfgAsync(ifIndex, value)` (declared via `extern` to avoid mxcfg include-path). Async (detached thread) so the single SNMP/AgentX task isn't blocked on the HTTP round-trip. ifAdminStatus up(1)/down(2)==CFA_IF_UP/DOWN, pass through. CAVEAT: `PortSetAdminStatus2MxCfg` handles PHYSICAL PORTS only (portTable, URI built as ifIndex-1). port-channel / L3-VLAN ifIndex need the other URI shapes from `ies-auto-mibs/.../uHandle_ifmib_ifTable_ifAdminStatus`: `/api/v1/setting/data/laSettings/portChannelTable/<idx>/enable` and `/ipInterface/l3VlanIfTable/<idx>/adminStatusUpEnable` (physical port = `/ifmib/portTable/<port-1>/enable`, body bool true/false). Fire-and-forget: PATCH failure not reported to SNMP SET result.

**Q1 — AgentX session drops under rapid/bursty requests; only disable/enable snmpsubagent recovers.** Root cause = TCP stream framing treated as datagram (NOT mem-pool exhaustion, which only drops packets and self-recovers). `snxtrans.c:SnxTransTcpRcvPacket` does a single `recv(sock, buf, SNX_MAX_MTU)` and treats it as one message; `SnxMainProcessRcvdPkt`'s `SNX_MUL_REQ_PKT` loop handles multiple WHOLE PDUs but discards a partial trailing PDU → inbound stream desyncs. `snxtrans.c:SnxTransTcpTxPacket` only checks `send()<0`, so a partial write (`0<ret<len`, common under master backpressure) is treated as success → outbound stream truncated → master closes session. Fresh socket (disable→enable, `SnxTransDeInit`) re-aligns the byte stream → recovery. FIXED 2026-06-25 (snxtrans.c + snxdef.h): added `SnxTransTcpRecvN` (recv EXACTLY n bytes, poll(POLLIN) on EAGAIN); rewrote `SnxTransTcpRcvPacket` to read the 20-byte header, parse payload_len via `SnxCodeGet4ByteData` (offset 16, byte order from flags byte offset 2), then read exactly payload → returns one complete PDU (no over/under-read). Rewrote `SnxTransTcpTxPacket` to loop send() until the whole PDU is written, poll(POLLOUT) on EAGAIN. New snxdef.h consts SNX_AGENTX_HDR_FLAGS_OFFSET=2 / _PAYLOADLEN_OFFSET=16 / SNX_TRANS_POLL_TIMEOUT_MS=1000; `#include <poll.h>`. BONUS: old send-fail path did `SelAddWrFd → SnxTransTcpOutSocket → SNX_TRANS_RDY_EVT → SnxMainOpenSession`, i.e. every backpressure partial-send reopened the AgentX session (session churn under load) — now gone. Tradeoff: one PDU per read event (the SNX_MUL_REQ_PKT batch loop in SnxMainProcessRcvdPkt is now never hit but harmless); add batching later if throughput needs it. Still to verify on DUT: rapid snmpbulkwalk/snmpget storm on ifTable/ifXTable keeps 705 ESTABLISHED (no manual disable/enable). Secondary contributor (not addressed): master `agentXTimeout 5`/`agentXRetries 1` under single-SNMP-task saturation.

